# Song working directories. Audio and build products stay out of git; the small
# hand-authored files (lyrics.txt, overrides.json, lyrics.timing.json) are worth
# keeping in version control — lyrics.timing.json in particular holds the sung
# timings recovered from burned-in subtitles, and re-running the OCR is slow.
songs/**/_in/
songs/**/*.mp4
songs/**/*.mov
songs/**/*.mkv
songs/**/*.mp3
songs/**/*.wav
songs/**/*.m4a
songs/**/*.flac
songs/**/stems/
songs/**/build/
songs/**/dist/
songs/**/build
songs/**/dist

# ★ The one exception: the sample song's audio IS committed.
#
# Everything above is inherited from the private repo, where "no audio in git"
# is absolute — that material belongs to other people. This repository ships
# exactly one song, and it belongs to the author: *Trempe-moi*, music generated
# with Suno, lyrics written by him.
#
# Without this line a fresh clone gets `lyrics.txt` and no audio, and the very
# first command the README teaches fails. That is the whole reason the song is
# here: so you can make something real before you go looking for your own
# material. Caught 2026-08-16, before the first push — the end-to-end check had
# been run against the *generated directory*, where the file is present on disk,
# rather than against a fresh clone, where it was not.
!songs/05-trempe-moi/source.mp3

# Job directories created by the local web shell (`murripple serve`):
# songs/web-<timestamp>-<original name>/. That is one person making one song on
# their own machine, not a work belonging to the repository.
songs/web-*/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.uv/
*.egg-info/

# Node
node_modules/
renderer/dist/

# Video export intermediates
video/frames/
*.mp4

# macOS
.DS_Store
